[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Requested ordinary analysis execution

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Bounded extension over the existing generated ANTLR grammar, immutable parameter evaluator, selected circuit lowering and one-shot public SimulationClient. No production dependency was added. Reuse decision: existing public OP/AC/transient wire requests satisfy this slice; source-sweep execution composes existing OP requests instead of adding a second simulator or parser. Existing SpiceSharp/ngspice qualification remains independent oracle work, not an authorized runtime migration.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-REQUESTED-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Ordered original ordinary analysis directives
STATEMENT: >>>
Prepare every supported root .op, single-source .dc, .ac lin/dec/oct and .tran directive in physical source order, retaining repeated directives with unique identities and original source ranges. Evaluate scalar fields through existing parameter semantics. Publish no partial program when a directive or physical instruction is unsupported.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: dotnet/Simulator.Syntax/AnalysisSyntax.cs, DeclarationExtraction.cs, DeclarationCatalog.cs; dotnet/Simulator.Frontend/RequestedAnalysis.cs. Verification: RequestedAnalysisTests.cs and RequestedAnalysisNativeTests.cs. Unmodeled controls, nested analyses, nested DC sweep and UIC are explicit refusals. Validated finite analysis controls are specified in requested-control-profile.sdoc. Bounded linear node .IC and separate reporting windows are specified in requested-initial-conditions.sdoc. Reporting/observation omissions remain explicit metadata and are not executed measurements.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-REQUESTED-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Fresh execution and atomic operation failure
STATEMENT: >>>
Execute the prepared analyses through the public client, in order, with a fresh engine process for each request. Execute every prepared point, preserve one outcome per point and operation, withhold partial successful payloads when any point in an operation fails, continue subsequent operations and propagate cancellation.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
DC explicitly uses fresh OP at every coordinate; this is not continuation or nonlinear hysteresis equivalence. Transport errors and engine failures remain distinct. No command interpreter, control-flow, arbitrary model or whole-corpus execution completeness is claimed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FRONTEND-REQUESTED-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Requested transient defaults and bounded grids
STATEMENT: >>>
Keep original transient TSTEP-dependent source defaults separate from the integration maximum step. Use explicit TMAX when supplied, otherwise min(TSTEP,(TSTOP-TSTART)/50) for supported reporting windows. Bound sweep expansion before allocation and reject invalid directions, zero DC steps and unsupported analysis options explicitly.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Existing backward-Euler runtime emits its accepted computational samples. Native adaptive sample grids differ; numerical comparison interpolates independent oracle values without claiming identical internal grids or integration methods. AC LIN2 follows the documented two-point grid; local ngspice47+ emits one point, retained as an oracle discrepancy rather than our requested grid contract.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-GOAL-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-ANALYSIS-TF-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Selected DC voltage transfer and port impedances
STATEMENT: >>>
A selected transfer shall bind up to sixteen root .tf V(output[,reference]) voltage-source directives in source order against the same prepared circuit. The selected input source shall be independently perturbed about its original DC bias with all other sources held fixed. The result shall report incremental voltage gain, input impedance from current drawn from the input source, and output impedance from a separate differential test-current injection. The result shall require finite derivatives and agreement at two perturbation scales. It shall represent zero incremental input current explicitly and refuse invalid ports, unsupported circuit contracts, failed probes and unstable derivatives.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: TransferFunctionSelection and scripts/Run-TransferFunction.cs. The derivative is a central finite difference with 100/50 uV input and 100/50 nA output perturbations. Stability compares derivatives with 0.1 percent relative tolerance plus floors of 1e-6 V/V, 1e-13 S and 1e-4 ohm. The check measures numerical consistency across scales. Nonlinear accuracy requires circuit-specific evidence. Root control blocks and hysteretic switches refuse this profile. Other analyses are outside the standalone selection. Requested-corpus dispatch and sensitivity remain separate.
<<<

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Windows verification on cbc2ac7 plus this change used dotnet test dotnet/Simulator.Frontend.Tests --filter FullyQualifiedName~TransferFunctionTests --collect "XPlat Code Coverage". Three tests passed with zero skips. The divider gain 2/3 and impedances 3000 and 666.6666667 ohms matched the analytical result and ngspice 47+ ASCII RAW on LU and Faer. An intentional reversal of input-current polarity failed both provider tests with negative 3000 ohms. Coverlet reported 86.04 percent lines and 59.61 percent branches for the handwritten selection class, and 84.21/54.54 percent for the main async state machine. Native coverage, fuzz and randomized properties were outside this run.

The unchanged RSpice general/diffpair.cir input SHA-256 is 7B8130123CB74140AC247CA8B9B0F50AEE0389B397AC9A4505493CDA225BB76B. The ngspice batch oracle recorded gains -0.11034131937 for VCM and -87.8473846657 for VDM, plus a 576-column sensitivity result. The standalone selector refused Q1 at line 10 with unsupported_bjt_profile due to VA=50. This run therefore establishes no diffpair agreement. Artifacts: E:/Artifacts/Spice-diffpair-20261109T172338.
<<<
